IMPORT prelude

-- LAYER 1: the regulative rules (PARTY / MUST / MAY / WITHIN / HENCE / LEST) of the provisions that give a named party a duty or a permission with a time limit
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025(c)(8), (j), (k)(2) and (k)(4), and 7 U.S.C. 2028(b)(1) and (b)(2); usc07-ch51.txt is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- A time is a number of days: a rule runs from the day the event that opens its window happens, and a #TRACE starts at 0 on that day.
-- #TRACE results cannot be asserted on the stable binary (NOTES.md, What the stable binary does not accept), so each rule here has a twin in the decision-function modules:
-- snap5-s2025-c2.l4 for (c)(8), snap5-s2025-k.l4 for (k) and snap5-s2028.l4 for s 2028, and snap5-tests-s2025-duties.l4 asserts the twin on the same facts beside each #TRACE.
-- A deadline extended for cause shown ((c)(8)(I)) is not in these rules: the twins take it as an input.
-- No rule here has a LEST that the text states: the text says what a party must do and by when, and says nothing of the consequence of missing it, so each LEST is a plain BREACH BY the party who missed, with the clause as the reason.

§ `s 2025(c)(8) The appeal of a payment claim or liability amount`

DECLARE `s 2025(c)(8) actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency`
    `s 2025(c)(8) the Secretary`
    `s 2025(c)(8) the administrative law judge`

DECLARE `s 2025(c)(8) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(c)(8)(D)(i) submit a notice of appeal`
    `s 2025(c)(8)(D)(ii) submit evidence in support of the appeal`
    `s 2025(c)(8)(E) submit responsive evidence`
    `s 2025(c)(8)(F) submit rebuttal evidence`
    `s 2025(c)(8)(G) decide the appeal`

-- Day 0 is the day the State agency receives a notice of the claim or liability amount. The responsive and rebuttal evidence exist; the rule is the one for a State agency that submits rebuttal evidence.
-- src:2027 | (D) A State agency desiring to appeal a payment claim or liability amount determined under subparagraph (C) shall submit to an administrative law judge—
-- src:2028 | (i) a notice of appeal, not later than 10 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount; and
-- src:2029 | (ii) evidence in support of the appeal of the State agency, not later than 60 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount.
-- src:2030 | (E) Not later than 60 days after a State agency submits evidence in support of the appeal, the Secretary shall submit responsive evidence to the administrative law judge to the extent such evidence exists.
-- src:2031 | (F) Not later than 30 days after the Secretary submits responsive evidence, the State agency shall submit rebuttal evidence to the administrative law judge to the extent such evidence exists.
-- src:2032 | (G) The administrative law judge, after an evidentiary hearing, shall decide the appeal—
-- src:2033 | (i) not later than 60 days after receipt of rebuttal evidence submitted by the State agency; or
-- src:2034 | (ii) if the State agency does not submit rebuttal evidence, not later than 90 days after the State agency submits the notice of appeal and evidence in support of the appeal.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(D) to (G) a State agency appeals a payment claim (src:2027-2034)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(c)(8) actor` `s 2025(c)(8) act`
`s 2025(c)(8)(D) to (G) a State agency appeals a payment claim` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency`
        MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(D)(i) submit a notice of appeal`
        WITHIN 10
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency` BECAUSE "no notice of appeal within 10 days of receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency`
        MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(D)(ii) submit evidence in support of the appeal`
        WITHIN 60
        HENCE (PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) the Secretary`
            MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(E) submit responsive evidence`
            WITHIN 60
            HENCE (PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency`
                MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(F) submit rebuttal evidence`
                WITHIN 30
                HENCE (PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) the administrative law judge`
                    MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(G) decide the appeal`
                    WITHIN 60
                    LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) the administrative law judge` BECAUSE "no decision within 60 days after receipt of rebuttal evidence")
                LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency` BECAUSE "no rebuttal evidence within 30 days after the Secretary submitted responsive evidence")
            LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) the Secretary` BECAUSE "no responsive evidence within 60 days after the State agency submitted evidence in support of the appeal")
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) a State agency` BECAUSE "no evidence in support of the appeal within 60 days of receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount")

-- Day 0 is the day the State agency has submitted both the notice of appeal and the evidence in support of the appeal.
-- src:2034 | (ii) if the State agency does not submit rebuttal evidence, not later than 90 days after the State agency submits the notice of appeal and evidence in support of the appeal.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(G)(ii) no rebuttal evidence: 90 days after the notice and evidence (src:2034)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(c)(8) actor` `s 2025(c)(8) act`
`s 2025(c)(8)(G)(ii) the administrative law judge decides when no rebuttal evidence is submitted` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2025(c)(8) the administrative law judge`
    MUST `s 2025(c)(8)(G) decide the appeal`
    WITHIN 90
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(c)(8) the administrative law judge` BECAUSE "no decision within 90 days after the State agency submitted the notice of appeal and evidence in support of the appeal"

§ `s 2025(k) The determination, the reduction and the appeal`

DECLARE `s 2025(k) actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(k) the Secretary`
    `s 2025(k) the Secretary of Health and Human Services`
    `s 2025(k) the State`
    `s 2025(k) the administrative law judge`
    `s 2025(k) the Departmental Appeals Board`

DECLARE `s 2025(k) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(k)(2) make the determinations`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(A) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the determination`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) appeal the determination to an administrative law judge`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv)(I) make a final decision on the appeal`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv)(II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) appeal the decision to the Departmental Appeals Board`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii)(I) make a final decision on the appeal to the Board`
    `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii)(II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the Board decision`

-- Day 0 is June 23, 1998.
-- src:2340 | Not later than 180 days after June 23, 1998, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, in consultation with the Secretary of Agriculture and the States, shall, with respect to the base period for each State, determine—
@ref s 2025(k)(2) the determinations within 180 days after June 23, 1998 (src:2340)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(2) the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determinations` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2025(k) the Secretary of Health and Human Services`
    MUST `s 2025(k)(2) make the determinations`
    WITHIN 180
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the Secretary of Health and Human Services` BECAUSE "the determinations were not made within 180 days after June 23, 1998"

-- Day 0 is the day the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes the determination with respect to the State.
-- src:2352 | Not later than 5 days after the date on which the Secretary of Health and Human Services makes any determination required by paragraph (2) with respect to a State, the Secretary shall notify the chief executive officer of the State of the determination.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(A) the Secretary notifies the chief executive officer within 5 days (src:2352)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(4)(A) the Secretary notifies the chief executive officer of the State` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2025(k) the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2025(k)(4)(A) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the determination`
    WITHIN 5
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the Secretary` BECAUSE "the chief executive officer of the State was not notified within 5 days after the determination"

-- Day 0 is the day the State receives notice of the determination. A permission unused is not a breach.
-- src:2355 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (A) of a determination, the State may appeal the determination, in whole or in part, to an administrative law judge of the Department of Health and Human Services by filing an appeal with the administrative law judge.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the State may appeal within 60 days of notice (src:2355)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) the State appeals to an administrative law judge` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2025(k) the State`
    MAY `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(i) appeal the determination to an administrative law judge`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- Day 0 is the day the record is closed.
-- src:2361 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which the record is closed, the administrative law judge shall—
-- src:2362 | (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and
-- src:2363 | (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the judge decides and notifies within 60 days after the record is closed (src:2361-2363)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv) the administrative law judge decides and notifies` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 2025(k) the administrative law judge`
        MUST `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv)(I) make a final decision on the appeal`
        WITHIN 60
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the administrative law judge` BECAUSE "no final decision within 60 days after the record was closed")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 2025(k) the administrative law judge`
        MUST `s 2025(k)(4)(B)(iv)(II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision`
        WITHIN 60
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the administrative law judge` BECAUSE "the chief executive officer of the State was not notified within 60 days after the record was closed")

-- Day 0 is the day the State receives notice of the final decision of the administrative law judge. A permission unused is not a breach.
-- src:2366 | Not later than 30 days after the date on which a State receives notice under subparagraph (B) of a final decision, the State may appeal the decision, in whole or in part, to the Departmental Appeals Board established in the Department of Health and Human Services (referred to in this paragraph as the “Board”) by filing an appeal with the Board.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the State may appeal to the Board within 30 days (src:2366)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) the State appeals to the Departmental Appeals Board` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2025(k) the State`
    MAY `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(i) appeal the decision to the Departmental Appeals Board`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- Day 0 is the day the appeal is filed.
-- src:2370 | Not later than 60 days after the date on which the appeal is filed, the Board shall—
-- src:2371 | (I) make a final decision with respect to an appeal filed under clause (i); and
-- src:2372 | (II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the decision.
@ref s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the Board decides and notifies within 60 days after the appeal is filed (src:2370-2372)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2025(k) actor` `s 2025(k) act`
`s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii) the Board decides and notifies` MEANS
    (PARTY `s 2025(k) the Departmental Appeals Board`
        MUST `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii)(I) make a final decision on the appeal to the Board`
        WITHIN 60
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the Departmental Appeals Board` BECAUSE "no final decision within 60 days after the appeal was filed")
    RAND
    (PARTY `s 2025(k) the Departmental Appeals Board`
        MUST `s 2025(k)(4)(C)(iii)(II) notify the chief executive officer of the State of the Board decision`
        WITHIN 60
        LEST BREACH BY `s 2025(k) the Departmental Appeals Board` BECAUSE "the chief executive officer of the State was not notified within 60 days after the appeal was filed")

§ `s 2028(b) The Commonwealth's plan, audit and statement`

DECLARE `s 2028(b) actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth`
    `s 2028(b) the Secretary`

DECLARE `s 2028(b) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2028(b)(1)(A) submit a plan`
    `s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) approve or disapprove the plan`
    `s 2028(b)(2)(A) report the findings of the audit to the Secretary`
    `s 2028(b)(2)(B) provide the Secretary with a statement`

-- Day 0 is the day the trace starts; the deadline is the number of days from then to July 1.
-- src:2760 | (A) In order to receive payments under this chapter for any fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall have a plan for that fiscal year approved by the Secretary under this section. By July 1 of each year, if the Commonwealth wishes to receive payments, it shall submit a plan for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B) for the following fiscal year which—
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(A) the plan by July 1 (src:2760)
GIVEN `days from the start to July 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2028(b) actor` `s 2028(b) act`
`s 2028(b)(1)(A) the Commonwealth submits a plan` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth`
    MUST `s 2028(b)(1)(A) submit a plan`
    WITHIN `days from the start to July 1`
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth` BECAUSE "no plan was submitted by July 1"

-- Day 0 is the day the trace starts; the deadline is the number of days from then to August 1.
-- src:2767 | (i) The Secretary shall approve or disapprove any plan submitted pursuant to subparagraph (A) no later than August 1 of the year in which it is submitted. The Secretary shall approve any plan which complies with the requirements of subparagraph (A). If a plan is disapproved because it does not comply with any of the requirements of that paragraph the Secretary shall, except as provided in subparagraph (B)(ii), notify the appropriate agency in the Commonwealth that payments will not be made to it under subsection (a) for the fiscal year to which the plan applies until the Secretary is satisfied that there is no longer any such failure to comply, and until the Secretary is so satisfied, the Secretary will make no payments.
@ref s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) approve or disapprove no later than August 1 (src:2767)
GIVEN `days from the start to August 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2028(b) actor` `s 2028(b) act`
`s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary approves or disapproves the plan` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2028(b) the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2028(b)(1)(B)(i) approve or disapprove the plan`
    WITHIN `days from the start to August 1`
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2028(b) the Secretary` BECAUSE "the plan was neither approved nor disapproved by August 1"

-- Day 0 is the end of the fiscal year in which the audit is made.
-- src:2770 | (A) The Commonwealth shall provide for a biennial audit of expenditures under its program for the provision of the assistance described in subsection (a)(2)(B), and within 120 days of the end of each fiscal year in which the audit is made, shall report to the Secretary the findings of such audit.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(A) report the audit findings within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year (src:2770)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2028(b) actor` `s 2028(b) act`
`s 2028(b)(2)(A) the Commonwealth reports the findings of the audit` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth`
    MUST `s 2028(b)(2)(A) report the findings of the audit to the Secretary`
    WITHIN 120
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth` BECAUSE "the findings of the audit were not reported within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year"

-- Day 0 is the end of the fiscal year.
-- src:2771 | (B) Within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year, the Commonwealth shall provide the Secretary with a statement as to whether the payments received under subsection (a) for that fiscal year exceeded the expenditures by it during that year for which payment is authorized under this section, and if so, by how much, and such other information as the Secretary may require.
@ref s 2028(b)(2)(B) the statement within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year (src:2771)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 2028(b) actor` `s 2028(b) act`
`s 2028(b)(2)(B) the Commonwealth provides the Secretary with a statement` MEANS
    PARTY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth`
    MUST `s 2028(b)(2)(B) provide the Secretary with a statement`
    WITHIN 120
    LEST BREACH BY `s 2028(b) the Commonwealth` BECAUSE "no statement was provided within 120 days of the end of the fiscal year"
